{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm/pulls/6883","id":1991250067,"node_id":"PR_kwDOI7xefs52sBCT","html_url":"https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/6883","diff_url":"https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/6883.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/6883.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm/issues/6883","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm/pulls/6883/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm/pulls/6883/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm/issues/6883/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm/statuses/bd0fd76f766e105d2e1eb29dbf009a9ad7279f34","number":6883,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"[ Frontend ] Multiprocessing for OpenAI Server with `zeromq`","user":{"login":"robertgshaw2-redhat","id":114415538,"node_id":"U_kgDOBtHXsg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/114415538?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/robertgshaw2-redhat","html_url":"https://github.com/robertgshaw2-redhat","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robertgshaw2-redhat/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robertgshaw2-redhat/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robertgshaw2-redhat/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robertgshaw2-redhat/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robertgshaw2-redhat/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robertgshaw2-redhat/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robertgshaw2-redhat/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robertgshaw2-redhat/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robertgshaw2-redhat/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"RFC: https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/issues/6797\r\n\r\nSUMMARY:\r\n* Use multiprocessing for OpenAI Server such that it does not contend with `AsyncLLMEngine`\r\n* Use `zeromq` for networking between OAI process and `AsyncLLMEngine`\r\n* Currently uses pickling for python serialization, to update this to use protobufs in separate PR\r\n* Gives ~20% TPOT improvement for QPS 10 for `llama-8b-instruct` on H100 (550 input tokens, 150 output tokens)\r\n\r\nTODO:\r\n\r\n- [x] enabling aborting\r\n- [x] enable do_log_stats\r\n- [x] error handling\r\n- [x] refactor to use single socket\r\n- [x] use open port\r\n- [x] turn on the other OAI endpoints\r\n- [x] add flag to disable mp\r\n- [x] tokenizer \r\n- [x] guided decoding\r\n- [x] tracing\r\n- [x] make CI green\r\n\r\nPERFORMANCE:\r\n* `zeromq` based protocol is delivering speedup in high QPS scenario:\r\n*  Llama-3-8B-Instruct, 1xH100, 550 input tokens | 150 output tokens, 10 QPS, chunked prefill\r\n\r\n| Metric | `main` | `grpc` | `zmq + pickle` (this PR) | `zmq + protobuf` |\r\n| - | - | - | - | - |\r\n| TPOT (mean) | 70.74 | 64.15 | 57.35 | 54.54 |\r\n| TTFT (mean) | 687.69 | 450.05 | 298.09 | 269.01 |\r\n\r\n\r\nClear win + clear we should move forward with `zeromq`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nBenchmark script for reference:\r\n\r\n```bash\r\nMODEL=\"meta-llama/Meta-Llama-3-8B-Instruct\"\r\nTOTAL_SECONDS=60\r\nQPS_RATES=(\"10\")\r\n\r\nfor QPS in ${QPS_RATES[@]}; do\r\n    NUM_PROMPTS=$((TOTAL_SECONDS * QPS))\r\n    echo \"===== RUNNING NUM_PROMPTS = $NUM_PROMPTS QPS = $QPS =====\"\r\n\r\n    python3 benchmarks/benchmark_serving.py \\\r\n        --model $MODEL \\\r\n        --dataset-name sonnet --sonnet-input-len 550 --sonnet-output-len 150 --dataset-path benchmarks/sonnet.txt \\\r\n        --num-prompts $NUM_PROMPTS --request-rate $QPS\r\ndone\r\n```\r\n\r\n--- \r\n\r\nFOLLOW UP WORK:\r\n* Refactor how logits processors are handled. They should not belong to the API layer anymore, rather below the engine. Currently there are hacks around making it serializable. \r\n* Switch to using a `protobuf` communication layer for the RPC Server\r\n* Move detokenization to the OAI layer\r\n* Profile using `N` uvicorn processes + expose a flag\r\n* Support embedding models via RPC\r\n\r\n","labels":[{"id":7197733874,"node_id":"LA_kwDOI7xefs8AAAABrQSz8g","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm/labels/ready","name":"ready","description":"ONLY add when PR is ready to merge/full CI is needed","color":"ededed","default":false}],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2024-07-29T02:45:27Z","updated_at":"2024-08-03T02:04:35Z","closed_at":"2024-08-03T01:27:28Z","merged_at":"2024-08-03T01:27:28Z","merge_commit_sha":"ed812a73fae77bb520b739cfeaad36dbd61e2b03","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"neuralmagic:isolate-oai-server-process","ref":"isolate-oai-server-process","repo":{"id":744696448,"node_id":"R_kgDOLGMqgA","name":"nm-vllm","full_name":"neuralmagic/nm-vllm","owner":{"login":"neuralmagic","id":68670575,"node_id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjY4NjcwNTc1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/68670575?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/neuralmagic","html_url":"https://github.com/neuralmagic","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neuralmagic/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neuralmagic/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neuralmagic/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neuralmagic/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neuralmagic/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neuralmagic/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neuralmagic/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neuralmagic/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neuralmagic/received_events","